<article class="env-corollary" id="F587">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F587">Corollary <span data-tag="F587">6.3.4.7</span>.</a> The $\infty $-category $\RGeom $ admits small limits. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollaries <a href="/tag/29B8" data-tag="29B8">4.2.3.11</a> and <a href="/tag/71B3" data-tag="71B3">4.4.2.4</a>, it suffices to show that $\RGeom $ admits filtered limits, a final object, and pullbacks. The existence of filtered limits follows from Theorem <a href="/tag/2B2C" data-tag="2B2C">6.3.3.1</a>, the existence of a final object follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/731D" data-tag="731D">6.3.4.1</a>, and the existence of pullbacks follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/02CA" data-tag="02CA">6.3.4.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>